             if ips:
                 return sorted(ips)[0]
+        # Containment pass: a host's address inside the requested subnet, in
+        # the form every other layer of ceph uses (pick_address.cc walks
+        # getifaddrs() and tests membership). Without it a spec naming an
+        # aggregate can never match a host-scoped address, whose key is a /32.
+        # Flatten to (interface, address) and sort by that pair: the map
+        # key is a route destination and can be unrelated to the address
+        # it holds, so ordering by key would let an unrelated route decide
